                "entry_id": "1b66f0c0-1afc-3083-82ab-8af81f109b6a",
                "word": "nunciature",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f18dbb9b-0b70-4692-95fb-94ea14182ab8",
                        "entry_id": "1b66f0c0-1afc-3083-82ab-8af81f109b6a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nunciatures"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "378797e4-61f0-3b86-bee8-fba1bcede11b",
                        "entry_id": "1b66f0c0-1afc-3083-82ab-8af81f109b6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The status or rank of a nuncio (diplomatic representative of the Roman Catholic Church)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "417c58f8-a44e-45ed-a8b9-a84b78f09aee",
                                "sense_id": "378797e4-61f0-3b86-bee8-fba1bcede11b",
                                "text": "Does their role include the bringing of the message of Christ in the political life of the country to which they are ambassadors? A clarification of the role of nunciature is necessary to maintain this \"appropriate communication.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0996ef23-d3ff-371d-a5f7-94c97b02850b",
                        "entry_id": "1b66f0c0-1afc-3083-82ab-8af81f109b6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The building and staff of a nuncio; the equivalent of an embassy for the Holy See."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e7c99aa-ac2d-43cf-95ca-c0a1804d785b",
                                "sense_id": "0996ef23-d3ff-371d-a5f7-94c97b02850b",
                                "text": "This was the prelate chosen by the new Pope, Innocent X., for the nunciature in Ireland: a man of noble birth, in the fifty-third year of his age, of uncertain bodily health, of great learning, especially as a canonist, of a fiery Italian temperament[…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f055436-8e05-4680-bd0a-46bab881d445",
                                "sense_id": "0996ef23-d3ff-371d-a5f7-94c97b02850b",
                                "text": "His ecclesiastical appointments showed how rapidly he had made his way, how supple was his mind: first of all secretary to the nunciature at Lisbon; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0fcc7cd-f33f-4eb9-bc54-5032d6315478",
                                "sense_id": "0996ef23-d3ff-371d-a5f7-94c97b02850b",
                                "text": "During the first winter of the war, a junior officer in the nunciature to Italy was summoned to the foreign ministry by the chef de cabinet of Foreign Minister Galeazzo Ciano to review some matter of ecclesiastical property."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de9cc27f-879c-4987-8688-4230aac19e43",
                                "sense_id": "0996ef23-d3ff-371d-a5f7-94c97b02850b",
                                "text": "Seeing as the meeting happened at the nunciature in Washington, it could only have happened with the approval and participation of the nuncio, Archbishop Carlo Maria Vigano."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afcc4020-bf98-3342-b4f7-0d94ba4b8254",
                        "entry_id": "1b66f0c0-1afc-3083-82ab-8af81f109b6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The term of service of a nuncio."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc519a4e-1835-4d54-a7b1-34258c05b5c3",
                                "sense_id": "afcc4020-bf98-3342-b4f7-0d94ba4b8254",
                                "text": "At the same time he had certainly searched documents, studied encyclical letters, based his sketch upon facts: first Leo's religious education at Rome, then his brief nunciature at Brussels, and afterwards his long episcopate at Perugia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f07eb64-0d94-4ca4-b4a1-560bb8742435",
                                "sense_id": "afcc4020-bf98-3342-b4f7-0d94ba4b8254",
                                "text": "The Warsaw nuncio was content to preach a spirit of peace, and was severely taken to task by the Polish press during the summer of 1920. This cast something of a shadow over the final period of his nunciature."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
